                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2773: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-11T19:00:00-05:00">January 11, 1933—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Department’s telegram No. 4, January 10, 1 p.m., Chaco. Foreign Office states
                    that Chilean plan being discussed with the Ambassador today and that in all
                    likelihood Peru will accept it entirely.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
